# The golden files under kumagen are compared byte for byte with what the
# generator writes, so they have to arrive the way they were committed rather
# than with the line endings of whatever machine checked them out.
*.golden -text

# Same for the compressed blocks in compress/snappy/testdata and the bytes they
# have to come back as. The bytes are the test, and a checkout that turns one
# line ending into two has changed both what went in and what came out.
*.raw -text
*.snappy -text
